armdeck: a switch for the blank layer behind the hidden Steam overlay

On a session backend gamescope composites a blank full-screen layer in the
Steam overlay's place while the overlay is hidden (upstream fe3dbc6b), so
the first frame of the overlay does not stutter. On the OnePlus 8 every
frame is composited on the GPU anyway (the panel is rotated and the SM8250
display planes cannot rotate 90 degrees), so that layer is one more
texture read and blend per output pixel on every frame, in every game.
ConVar paint_blank_overlay_plane (default on, the upstream behaviour)
leaves it out when cleared; ARMDECK_NO_BLANK_OVERLAY=1 makes the default
off, and gamescopectl can switch it at runtime for an A/B test. The Steam
overlay itself still paints when shown.

Idea and ConVar name from Nova-Deck's os-build (patch 0037 by Philippe
Simons, 2026-10-26), where on SM8250 with planes the layer halved the frame
rate; written again here for 3.16.29. Not yet measured on the OnePlus 8.

--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -3076,6 +3076,12 @@
 gamescope::ConVar<bool> cv_paint_primary_plane{ "paint_primary_plane", true };
